  "summary": "On 1 October 331 BCE Alexander of Macedon defeated the Persian army of Darius III at Gaugamela, also called the Battle of Arbela. Darius fled and the Persian line broke. Sources describe Alexander as then holding Babylon, Persepolis and Susa, while Darius was later deposed and killed by his nobles.",
